Clax is free software. Each part is licensed under one of the licenses below,
whose full texts are in the LICENSES/ directory:

  GPL-2.0-only     GNU General Public License, version 2 only
                   (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt)
  AGPL-3.0-only    GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only
                   (LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt)
  LGPL-2.1-only    GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 only
                   (LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-only.txt)
  0BSD             Zero-Clause BSD License
                   (LICENSES/0BSD.txt)

"Only" means what it says: no later version of the GNU licenses applies,
and "any later version" wording in the license texts themselves does not
apply to Clax.

Which license covers which part:

  GPL-2.0-only                    The local programs and everything that
                                  ships only with them:
    crates/clax-cli
    crates/clax-commands
    crates/clax-hooks
    crates/clax-embedded
    crates/clax-fake-exe
    plugins/                      the agent plugins, including plugins/pi
    web/extension/                the browser extension
    apps/clax_app                 the Clax app, including its home app
                                  (apps/clax_app/home), except its
                                  starter kit (below)
    scripts/, demo/, docs/, and every file not listed below

  GPL-2.0-only OR AGPL-3.0-only   Code shared by the local programs and the
                                  hosted service; you may use it under
                                  either license:
    crates/clax-core
    crates/clax-store
    crates/clax-sample
    crates/clax-realtime
    crates/clax-http
    crates/clax-server
    crates/clax-mcp
    crates/clax-rt
    crates/clax-git
    crates/clax-content-git
    crates/clax-bot-sandbox
    crates/clax-bot-js
    crates/clax-testkit

  MIT                             Patched copies of third-party crates:
    third_party/clax-rquickjs-sys   rquickjs-sys and rquickjs-core (MIT,
    third_party/clax-rquickjs-core  as their manifests say) and QuickJS
                                    (MIT, the text in
                                    third_party/clax-rquickjs-sys/quickjs/LICENSE)

  AGPL-3.0-only                   The web application and the hosted service:
    crates/clax-worker            (including crates/clax-worker/vfs)
    web/                          except web/extension/, web/bridge/,
                                  web/overlay/ and web/sdk/

  LGPL-2.1-only                   The SDK and the overlay a deployer's app
                                  embeds, and the bridge code they are
                                  built from, so the apps that use them
                                  may be under any license:
    web/sdk/
    web/overlay/
    web/bridge/

  0BSD                            The Clax app's starter kit, which the app
                                  copies into the apps people make with it,
                                  so they carry no obligation from it:
    apps/clax_app/assets/kit      Clax's own files in it; its vendored
                                  third-party files (preact.js, dates.js,
                                  icons.js) keep their own licenses, which
                                  apps/clax_app/assets/kit/LICENSES.txt
                                  holds

A package's own metadata (the `license` field of its Cargo.toml or
package.json) names the same license as this list. web/package.json covers
all of web/, including web/extension/, web/sdk/, web/overlay/ and
web/bridge/, so it names all three of their licenses. A Dart package's
pubspec.yaml has no license field (pub reads the package's LICENSE file):
apps/clax_app/LICENSE carries the app's license.

